# Engine wave 2, E6. A record's hashCode differed from the pinned JDK's: record Student(String name, int score) gave
# new Student("Ada", 88).hashCode() = 2,036,571 on the fork and 2,035,610 on the JDK, and record Point(double x,
# double y) gave new Point(3, 4).hashCode() = 17,302,465 and 17,301,504, so a HashSet or HashMap of records iterated in
# another order on the two (runtime/test/cases.mjs, the E6 cases).
#   - The rule, from the pinned JDK run black box on 76 records of zero to four components: every primitive type as a
#     component (-0.0, NaN, infinities, negative numbers and longs past 32 bits among the values), String, Integer, a
#     List, another record and null. A record with no components hashes to 0. Otherwise its hash is h = 31 * h + c
#     from h = 0, over the components in declaration order, where c is the component's own hash as its wrapper type
#     gives it (Integer.hashCode, Long.hashCode, Double.hashCode, Boolean.hashCode and the rest) or as
#     Objects.hashCode gives it for a reference (0 for null). That matched all 76; starting from 1 matched none, and
#     taking the components in reverse order matched only the records of one component or none.
#   - TeaVM emulates the ObjectMethods bootstrap that a record's equals, hashCode and toString call (javac emits an
#     invokedynamic to it) in its classlib's ObjectMethodsSubstitutor, and its hashCode started from 1. Its hash of
#     each component was already the JDK's: the same probe printed every component's own hash identically on both.
#     So every record's hash was off by exactly 31 to the power of its number of components (961 for two).
#   - Now it starts from 0. Nothing else changes: on both, a record's hashCode reads its fields and never calls an
#     accessor the record overrides.
#
# Written from TeaVM's own source (classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/record/ObjectMethodsSubstitutor.java
# and the bootstrap's registration in classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/JCLPlugin.java) and the pinned
# JDK's observed output; no OpenJDK source was opened (clean room, D14). Written by a subagent (Claude Opus 5.5), a
# language model whose training may include OpenJDK, so the patch was read for names or structure that look recalled
# rather than derived: it adds no name and changes one constant in TeaVM's own code, to the value the probes show.
#
# Applies to: github.com/konsoletyper/teavm tag 0.13.1 (b3a245b7). The only other patch that touches
# ObjectMethodsSubstitutor is teavm-0025, which changes other lines of it (equals); each applies with or without the
# other.

diff --git a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/record/ObjectMethodsSubstitutor.java b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/record/ObjectMethodsSubstitutor.java
index d4ac694..e8b4c62 100644
--- a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/record/ObjectMethodsSubstitutor.java
+++ b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/record/ObjectMethodsSubstitutor.java
@@ -110,7 +110,9 @@ public class ObjectMethodsSubstitutor implements BootstrapMethodSubstitutor {
     private ValueEmitter substituteHashCode(DynamicCallSite callSite, ProgramEmitter pe) {
         ValueEmitter thisVar = callSite.getArguments().get(0);
         String names = callSite.getBootstrapArguments().get(1).getString();
-        ValueEmitter resultVar = pe.constant(1);
+        // teavm-fork: from 0, as on the pinned JDK. A record with no components hashes to 0, and each component in
+        // turn makes the hash 31 * (the hash so far) + (its own hash).
+        ValueEmitter resultVar = pe.constant(0);
 
         int argIndex = 2;
         int index = 0;
